\section{Discussion and limitations}
On Iris, LR and tuned kNN cannot be told apart (difference \Dlo{} to \Dhi{} pp). This is one small, nearly separable dataset with accuracies near the ceiling, so it says nothing about which method is better in general; only $k$ is tuned while LR keeps $C=1$, as the design prescribes; the corrected interval is an approximation; and cross-validation estimates accuracy averaged over training sets, not that of one fitted model \citep{bates2024}.
Fold accuracies move in steps of $1/30$, hence the many ties. Code and results are in \texttt{report/}.

